iption=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>You are given an arr=
ay of integers&nbsp;<code>nums</code>, there is a sliding window of size <c=
ode>k</code> which is moving from the very left of the array to the very ri=
ght. You can only see the <code>k</code> numbers in the window. Each time t=
he sliding window moves right by one position.</p>

<p>Return <em>the max sliding window</em>.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [1,3,-1,-3,5,3,6,7], k =3D 3
<strong>Output:</strong> [3,3,5,5,6,7]
<strong>Explanation:</strong>=20
Window position                Max
---------------               -----
[1  3  -1] -3  5  3  6  7       <strong>3</strong>
 1 [3  -1  -3] 5  3  6  7       <strong>3</strong>
 1  3 [-1  -3  5] 3  6  7      <strong> 5</strong>
 1  3  -1 [-3  5  3] 6  7       <strong>5</strong>
 1  3  -1  -3 [5  3  6] 7       <strong>6</strong>
 1  3  -1  -3  5 [3  6  7]      <strong>7</strong>
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [1], k =3D 1
<strong>Output:</strong> [1]
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D nums.length &lt;=3D 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>
	<li><code>-10<sup>4</sup> &lt;=3D nums[i] &lt;=3D 10<sup>4</sup></code></l=
i>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D k &lt;=3D nums.length</code></li>
</ul>
